{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire","id":786876,"title":"What does Beast blood do to a vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-15T13:01:41-08:00","id":786876,"title":"What does Beast blood do to a vampire?","content":"Hi! Long time OP lurker, had to create an account as I fell in love with Beast.<br /> <br /> So, unless I missed it the core book has nothing on what Beast blood does to a vampire. Any ideas? I was thinking it could increase the chance of fear frenzy in vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:12:00-08:00","id":786884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire#post786876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Long time OP lurker, had to create an account as I fell in love with Beast.<br /> <br /> So, unless I missed it the core book has nothing on what Beast blood does to a vampire. Any ideas? I was thinking it could increase the chance of fear frenzy in vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense. They would probably also have nightmares during daysleep, but I don't think that would have any mechanical effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:14:42-08:00","id":786887,"title":"","content":"Allows BP 4+ Kindred sup on something other than other Kindred, if they take the appropriate Merit. That's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:17:40-08:00","id":787016,"title":"","content":"I think they ditched the whole &quot;supernatural blood makes Kindred high&quot; thing with the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:01:29-08:00","id":787064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787016#post787016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they ditched the whole &quot;supernatural blood makes Kindred high&quot; thing with the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually loved that re: mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T22:44:41-08:00","id":787166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire#post786876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Long time OP lurker, had to create an account as I fell in love with Beast.<br /> <br /> So, unless I missed it the core book has nothing on what Beast blood does to a vampire. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably something like the tunnel scene from Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate Factory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T04:11:39-08:00","id":787263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787016#post787016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they ditched the whole &quot;supernatural blood makes Kindred high&quot; thing with the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a real shame, because it was great fluff. I like the idea that Vampires that feed on supernaturals without the appropriate Unnatural Affinity Merit receive nourishment as if they drank human blood and gain a negative Condition until they manage to use up the Vitae gained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T04:33:08-08:00","id":787273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787263#post787263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is a real shame, because it was great fluff. I like the idea that Vampires that feed on supernaturals without the appropriate Unnatural Affinity Merit receive nourishment as if they drank human blood and gain a negative Condition until they manage to use up the Vitae gained.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% Agreed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:26:58-08:00","id":787778,"title":"","content":"First, as others have said, supernatural blood doesn't do anything to vampires by default in 2e. So, no Rage, no cackling madness, no pseudo-Disquiet, no inability to tell reality from fantasy apart. <br /> <br /> Secondly, I'd like to point out everything on that list I just mentioned was the old drawback for feeding on wolves, mages, prommies, and changelings, respectively. What happened was that, in each case, the vampire got a touch of the splat's drawbacks. Werewolves have rage issues, so vampires inherited it when they drank. Mages were all about hubris and the meglomania, and vamps got a taste of that. Same with disquiet when munching on a prommie, and Clairity issues when sipping on a 'ling. Drinking supernatural blood wasn't like drinking poison. It wasn't a punishment. It was adapting another's curse inside you to act more like the supernatural in question<br /> <br /> So, if you want to keep with the same things as vamps suffering from drinking supernat blood, then, when drinking from Beasts, it should reflect some of their innate weaknesses somehow. Beasts don't suffer from nightmares, they ARE the nightmares. That's their strength, not their weakness. It doesn't make sense for a vampire to suffer from it. <br /> <br /> So, what are the weaknesses of being a Beast? Heroes and Athenema, naturally. Hunger. So, a vampire who feeds from a Beast should either pick up temporary Banes for a while, or have a harder time resisting feeding their thirst for blood. Trigger wassil at a hair drop, or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T22:55:04-08:00","id":787869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787778#post787778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, as others have said, supernatural blood doesn't do anything to vampires by default in 2e. So, no Rage, no cackling madness, no pseudo-Disquiet, no inability to tell reality from fantasy apart.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I'd like to point out everything on that list I just mentioned was the old drawback for feeding on wolves, mages, prommies, and changelings, respectively. What happened was that, in each case, the vampire got a touch of the splat's drawbacks. Werewolves have rage issues, so vampires inherited it when they drank. Mages were all about hubris and the meglomania, and vamps got a taste of that. Same with disquiet when munching on a prommie, and Clairity issues when sipping on a 'ling. Drinking supernatural blood wasn't like drinking poison. It wasn't a punishment. It was adapting another's curse inside you to act more like the supernatural in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always wondered if Sin Eaters would cause vampires some kind of problem, given the plasm in their blood and all, if Vampires were affected by the blood they drink. Would the death energies therein affect the undead? Sin Eaters don't tend to have the same kind of weaknesses or problems that the other supernaturals have - if anything they're one of the harder splats to put down, even temporarily. Given that synergy is really the only thing that would suffer for them, and Vampires lack an appropriate stat, what would they suffer from?<br /> <br /> Apologies, I know this is about Beasts and that this would probably be a non-issue in 2e; I just couldn't help but ask given the subject was up and it had been on my mind for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-17-2015, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T03:21:40-08:00","id":787956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787869#post787869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wondered if Sin Eaters would cause vampires some kind of problem, given the plasm in their blood and all, if Vampires were affected by the blood they drink. Would the death energies therein affect the undead? Sin Eaters don't tend to have the same kind of weaknesses or problems that the other supernaturals have - if anything they're one of the harder splats to put down, even temporarily. Given that synergy is really the only thing that would suffer for them, and Vampires lack an appropriate stat, what would they suffer from?<br /> <br /> Apologies, I know this is about Beasts and that this would probably be a non-issue in 2e; I just couldn't help but ask given the subject was up and it had been on my mind for some time.</div> </div> </div> </div> GtSE is, for all intents and purposes, a game where you play a grim reaper. You are absolutely half-ghost-being here, much in the same way that werewolves are half-spirit, and not a mortal or a human anymore. And you are associated with a type of undead that is instrictively different than the vampiric Curse. So, yes, you would be affected by the plasm in the blood. In fact, as further proof, there's an effect on the vampire from drinking straight up ghost plasm. <br /> <br /> Geist is a strange game, in that it was designed to be a bare bones, open sandbox game that just gave you all the tools to use or not. So, its not that SEs don't have weaknesses to absorb, its that the high level of tinkering permitted by the game has made the less obvious and placed in strange locations. There is a bit of an assumption is that you'll be taking krewe banes and bans, much like an ephemeral entity would be developing the same banes and bans based on its nature, but players being who they are, tend to overlook them. SE's also have a &quot;weakness&quot; of being constantly badgered by ghosts to the point it takes concerted effort to block them out. There was one or two other things I brought up before, such as a draw to places near the Underworld or tied to a keystone/anchor of some type as well, but I don't remember the details. All the potential weaknesses are there, they're just not as obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T03:30:16-08:00","id":787959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787778#post787778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if you want to keep with the same things as vamps suffering from drinking supernat blood, then, when drinking from Beasts, it should reflect some of their innate weaknesses somehow. Beasts don't suffer from nightmares, they ARE the nightmares. That's their strength, not their weakness. It doesn't make sense for a vampire to suffer from it.<br /> <br /> So, what are the weaknesses of being a Beast? Heroes and Athenema, naturally. Hunger. So, a vampire who feeds from a Beast should either pick up temporary Banes for a while, or have a harder time resisting feeding their thirst for blood. Trigger wassil at a hair drop, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in the case of werewolves, there was also a bonus, in that their blood provided a lot more vitae for the health level. It wouldn't be out of keeping for the same to be true of Beasts<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T06:50:26-08:00","id":788049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=787959#post787959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least in the case of werewolves, there was also a bonus, in that their blood provided a lot more vitae for the health level. It wouldn't be out of keeping for the same to be true of Beasts<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts don't have superlative regeneration ability though, nor are their physical bodies necessarily enhanced by being Begotten.<br /> <br /> I do think that The Kiss would be an interesting way to deliver The Mother's Kiss to a vampire though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T07:10:52-08:00","id":788070,"title":"","content":"Beasts with Relentless Hunter have regeneration nearly on par with a werewolf, but that already provides mechanics for bonus Vitae insofar as the Beast will regenerate the 1L every thirty minutes instead of every two days, allowing them to viably sustain a friendly vamp indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T11:55:23-08:00","id":788252,"title":"","content":"Thanks all for answering! I particularly like MCN's idea. Beast blood making banes more dangerous to vampires sounds great.<br /> <br /> Also, my old favorite side effect was Promethean blood being half less nutritious and absolutely disgusting. But then I've always loved all things Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T05:15:20-08:00","id":788677,"title":"","content":"Oh, one thing that is explicitly mentioned in Beast is that their blood tastes very similar to that of Heroes. (Something vampires tend to find funnier than the Beasts or Heroes do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T10:02:07-08:00","id":788834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/786876-what-does-beast-blood-do-to-a-vampire?p=788677#post788677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, one thing that is explicitly mentioned in Beast is that their blood tastes very similar to that of Heroes. (Something vampires tend to find funnier than the Beasts or Heroes do).</div> </div> </div> </div>Parenthetical's been gone since the revisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T04:01:50-08:00","id":791476,"title":"","content":"I would like to say that 2nd doesn't actually state that supernatural blood doesn't have an effect on vampires, but like with some of the bullshit limitations due to their word count limit it was just one of the many things not included, just like how there is no actual mechanical examples of bloodlines. So I wouldn't be too hasty and say that there is no effect, we just haven't been shown any as of yet is all.","signature":"","edited":